The table structure information is ({database name: {schema name: [table name]}}): 
{'THELOOK_ECOMMERCE': {'THELOOK_ECOMMERCE': ['DISTRIBUTION_CENTERS', 'ORDERS', 'USERS', 'EVENTS', 'INVENTORY_ITEMS', 'PRODUCTS', 'ORDER_ITEMS']}}
Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns & potential usage  
• PRODUCTS."category": filter to the ‛Sleep & Lounge’ product category  
• PRODUCTS."id": joins to ORDER_ITEMS."product_id" to bring in cost & category  
• PRODUCTS."cost": unit cost of each SKU – summed for total monthly cost  
• PRODUCTS."retail_price": optional reference price (not needed for profit)  
• ORDER_ITEMS."sale_price": what the customer actually paid – summed for total monthly sales  
• ORDER_ITEMS."product_id": join key to PRODUCTS  
• ORDER_ITEMS."order_id": join key to ORDERS in order to double‑check order status  
• ORDER_ITEMS."status": keep only rows whose value = 'Complete'  
• ORDER_ITEMS."created_at": micro‑second epoch time the line‑item was created – used to restrict to 2023 and to derive the calendar month  
• ORDERS."order_id": join key to ORDER_ITEMS  
• ORDERS."status": make sure the full order is also marked ‘Complete’  
• ORDERS."created_at": alternative date field (use either item or order date)  

Main conditions that will be applied later  
1) PRODUCTS."category" ILIKE '%Sleep%Lounge%'  
2) ORDER_ITEMS."status" = 'Complete'  
3) ORDERS."status" = 'Complete'  
4) ORDER_ITEMS."created_at" BETWEEN 1672531200000000 /* 2023‑01‑01 */  
                              AND 1704067199999999 /* 2023‑12‑31 */  


Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20 each, all column names in double quotes).  
```sql
--Description: 1) See all distinct product categories that exist in the catalog
SELECT DISTINCT "category"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Quickly confirm the literal form of the “Sleep & Lounge” category text
SELECT DISTINCT "category"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS
WHERE "category" ILIKE '%Sleep%Lounge%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Sample products that belong to the Sleep & Lounge category
SELECT "id"          AS "product_id",
       "name",
       "brand",
       "cost",
       "retail_price",
       "category"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS
WHERE "category" ILIKE '%Sleep%Lounge%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Look at the distribution of order‑item statuses for Sleep & Lounge SKUs
SELECT DISTINCT oi."status"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS   oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS      p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE p."category" ILIKE '%Sleep%Lounge%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) Show a handful of completed Sleep & Lounge line‑items created in 2023
SELECT oi."id"              AS "order_item_id",
       oi."order_id",
       oi."product_id",
       oi."sale_price",
       oi."created_at"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS   oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS      p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE p."category" ILIKE '%Sleep%Lounge%'
  AND oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1672531200000000 AND 1704067199999999
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Cross‑check that the parent order is also marked Complete
SELECT oi."order_id",
       o."status"         AS "order_status",
       COUNT(*)           AS "item_cnt"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS   oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDERS        o
  ON o."order_id" = oi."order_id"
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS      p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE p."category" ILIKE '%Sleep%Lounge%'
  AND oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1672531200000000 AND 1704067199999999
GROUP BY oi."order_id", o."status"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Capture sales vs. cost per completed line‑item (first 20 rows)
SELECT oi."id"            AS "order_item_id",
       oi."order_id",
       oi."sale_price",
       p."cost"           AS "unit_cost",
       (oi."sale_price" - p."cost") AS "profit"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS   oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS      p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE p."category" ILIKE '%Sleep%Lounge%'
  AND oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1672531200000000 AND 1704067199999999
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Monthly aggregation: sales, cost, profit for 2023 Sleep & Lounge
SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at"/1e6), 'YYYY-MM') AS "month",
       SUM(oi."sale_price")                                  AS "total_sales",
       SUM(p."cost")                                         AS "total_cost",
       SUM(oi."sale_price" - p."cost")                       AS "total_profit"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS   oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS      p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE p."category" ILIKE '%Sleep%Lounge%'
  AND oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1672531200000000 AND 1704067199999999
GROUP BY TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at"/1e6), 'YYYY-MM')
ORDER BY "month"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Add number of completed orders (distinct order_id) to the monthly roll‑up
SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at"/1e6), 'YYYY-MM') AS "month",
       COUNT(DISTINCT oi."order_id")                         AS "complete_orders",
       SUM(oi."sale_price")                                  AS "total_sales",
       SUM(p."cost")                                         AS "total_cost",
       SUM(oi."sale_price" - p."cost")                       AS "total_profit"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS   oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS      p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE p."category" ILIKE '%Sleep%Lounge%'
  AND oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1672531200000000 AND 1704067199999999
GROUP BY TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at"/1e6), 'YYYY-MM')
ORDER BY "month"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final style query including profit‑to‑cost ratio for each 2023 month
SELECT TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at"/1e6), 'YYYY-MM')                  AS "month",
       COUNT(DISTINCT oi."order_id")                                          AS "complete_orders",
       SUM(oi."sale_price")                                                   AS "total_sales",
       SUM(p."cost")                                                          AS "total_cost",
       SUM(oi."sale_price" - p."cost")                                        AS "total_profit",
       CASE WHEN SUM(p."cost") = 0 THEN NULL
            ELSE ROUND(SUM(oi."sale_price" - p."cost") / SUM(p."cost"), 2)
       END                                                                    AS "profit_to_cost_ratio"
FROM THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.ORDER_ITEMS   oi
JOIN THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.THELOOK_ECOMMERCE.PRODUCTS      p
  ON p."id" = oi."product_id"
WHERE p."category" ILIKE '%Sleep%Lounge%'
  AND oi."status" = 'Complete'
  AND oi."created_at" BETWEEN 1672531200000000 AND 1704067199999999
GROUP BY TO_CHAR(TO_TIMESTAMP(oi."created_at"/1e6), 'YYYY-MM')
ORDER BY "month"
LIMIT 20;
```

